### Summary

As a SwiftHFR user, I want the same gesture or screen state to behave the same way in every section (Catégories, topics, Favoris, Messages, search, profile, reader), so that nothing I learnt in one tab surprises me in another.

This is the **behaviour** half of UX consistency:
- #572 covers the visual half (one list style, `RowTint`, `ListDensity`, reader tokens);
- #545 covers Liquid Glass.

Operator decision 2026-11-09 (M4).

### Scope

1. **Consistency matrix**, recorded as a section of `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md` (not a new document). One row per screen, one column per behaviour:
   - pull to refresh;
   - loading, empty and error states;
   - context menu on a row;
   - row swipes (legacy set in M4; the uniform set is LOT-177, M5);
   - the account/avatar menu (UXD-03, #425);
   - re-selecting a tab (UXD-04, #426);
   - haptics;
   - search entry.

   Each cell reads "same as the reference", "documented difference (GAP/UXD row)" or an open issue.
2. **Shared state components** in `App/SwiftHFR/`: one floating card (the same `.regularMaterial` + `RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 12)` is copied today in `TopicListView.swift:226`, `MessageListView.swift:102`, `LoadFailureView.swift:36`, `ReplyComposerView.swift:323`, `ReaderReplyFlow.swift:72`), and one loading / empty / error view, building on `LoadFailureView` and `ContentUnavailableView`. Its glass treatment follows #545.
3. **Measured gaps on `dev-swift` @ `5b3853a` (2026-11-06)**, to re-check:
   - `.refreshable` only in Messages, Navigation and Profile;
   - no `.sensoryFeedback`, although UXD-04 asks for a haptic;
   - no shared search entry.
4. **Parity gate:** the matrix becomes a criterion of LOT-164 (#254). Every row must be "consistent" or a documented difference.

### Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The matrix is in `GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`, with every cell decided.
- [ ] The floating card and the state view are shared; `git grep "RoundedRectangle(cornerRadius: 12)"` shows only the shared component.
- [ ] Pull to refresh and the state views behave the same in every list, or the difference is documented.
- [ ] LOT-164 (#254) names this matrix as a gate item.
- [ ] One Mac pass, light and dark, Dynamic Type XL.

Related: #572, #545, #425, #426, LOT-177 (#417, M5).

